Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 12:41:05 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] =?UTF-8?q?Under-ice=20coupling=20tests=20(issue=20#48):?=
 =?UTF-8?q?=20CATKE's=20surface=20TKE=20flux=20scaled=20by=20the=20open=20?=
 =?UTF-8?q?water;=20drag-based=20ice=E2=80=93ocean=20u=E2=98=85?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

[ocean] catke_under_ice multiplies CATKE's surface shear-driven TKE flux, Cᵂu★ u★³, by 1 − ℵ ("open_water") or
1 − tanh(10ℵ) ("tanh"), as NEMO 4 attenuates its surface TKE input under ice (nn_eice; Allende et al. 2024). It
replaces CATKE's TKE top boundary condition after the model is built, passing the sea-ice concentration in its
parameters.

[sea_ice] ice_ocean_friction_velocity = "drag" uses u★ = max(√Cᴰ |uⁱ − uᵒ|, 0.002 m/s) in the three-equation ice–ocean
heat and salt exchange instead of NumericalEarth's constant 0.002 m/s, as LIM2 (McPhee). NumericalEarth's
MomentumBasedFrictionVelocity is not used: it sees only the explicit part of the drag, −λ uⁱ, so its u★² is
Cᴰ |Δu| |uⁱ| rather than Cᴰ |Δu|².

Configs: config_smoke_test_under_ice.toml (100 km, 4 days, both options), and 30-day runs at 15 km
config_sep2005_30d_catke_ice_openwater.toml, config_sep2005_30d_catke_ice_tanh.toml,
config_sep2005_30d_ice_ustar_drag.toml.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01AbhhvmYEBvTrBMFfuX35Ju
